  "published": "2026-11-08T04:00:52.383Z",
  "readmeFile": "docs\\README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.0.5-alpha (2026-11-08) - 16 new nodes, 56 in all. Tier 1 of the coverage plan:\n      Touches, Crosses, Overlaps, Covers, CoveredBy, Relate, IsWithinDistance, SymmetricDifference,\n      ConvexHull, Reverse (NetTopologySuite.Operation); Envelope, InteriorPoint, Boundary, IsSimple,\n      NumPoints (NetTopologySuite.Geometry). And Outlines (NetTopologySuite.Geometry): one polyline\n      per ring or line, and every point. A Geometry now draws itself in the editor the way a GIS\n      draws it: hover a Geometry pin or make an IOBox of one and you see filled polygons with their\n      holes, lines, point markers, a map pin for a point, a Feature with every attribute listed under\n      it (VL.NetTopologySuite.HDE.vl, editor only). Every help patch shows its geometry that way;\n      new help patch HowTo Wrap points in a hull, six patches extended.\n\n      0.0.4-alpha (2026-10-18) - Tooltips rewritten to be short: every node now shows a one-line\n      summary, a sentence or two of usage and a line per pin on hover, instead of design notes.\n      No node changed. Same 40 nodes as 0.0.3-alpha.\n\n      0.0.3-alpha (2026-10-18) - Adds GetAttribute (NetTopologySuite.Feature): one\n      attribute by name, with Success instead of an exception. VL.NetTopologySuite.GeoJSON (formerly\n      VL.GeoJSON) depends on this version.\n\n      0.0.2-alpha (2026-10-17) - The nodes now live under NetTopologySuite.Geometry, .Operation, .IO,\n      .Feature, .Index and .Network instead of NTS.*, so searching the NodeBrowser for the package's\n      own name finds them. Patches made with 0.0.1-alpha keep working: a node resolves by name\n      within the referenced package. Also: Test-Install -FromNuGetOrg, and the README's install\n      section. No node added, removed or changed.\n\n      0.0.1-alpha (2026-09-26) - The first release, a prerelease. 39 nodes in six categories - NTS.Geometry,\n      NTS.Feature, NTS.Operation, NTS.IO, NTS.Index, NTS.Network - 126 tests, 15 help patches, and\n      F1 on every node opens one. Verified in vvvv gamma 7.4. Coordinates are copied on the way in\n      and out, so a geometry cannot be moved behind your back. Not ready for real work: the node\n      surface may still change between prereleases.",
